**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The item edits the Items panel sends besides AddItem and SetParameterState: a label, notes and a photo (the S7.2 brief: 'plus label, notes and photo edits'; 001 §I: an item has an optional photo (a kit file) and notes; the S7.1 mapper's request: a rename, photo or notes edit is its own member). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) ItemError.UnknownKitItemErr from step 213 MUST be reused unchanged; the copy mapping already consumes it. (2) On `Item` (step 215), beside `withParameterState` (step 234): `member this.withNotes (notes : ItemNotes) : Item` answers the item with those notes; `member this.withPhoto (photoOpt : KitRelativePath option) : Item` answers it with that photo, `None` removing the reference and never a file (001 §E 'Lab files are read-only for the app'); `member this.relabelledAmong (label : ItemLabel) (items : Item list) : Result<Item, ItemError>` answers `DuplicateItemLabelErr` naming both labels when an item of `items` with another `id` has a label whose `fileStem` equals the new one's ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`, the rule of `ItemDraft.addTo`, step 216), and otherwise the item with the new label; the item's own entry in `items` is ignored, so `lp1` may become `LP1`. None of the three changes the parameters, the revision or the history: like `withParameterState` they edit the working revision, and only `publishRevision` moves it (steps 234, 235). (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ItemIdProvider = { mintItemId : unit -> ItemId }`, the provider that mints a new item's identity (AGENTS.md: ambient effects are injected as provider records, as `ClockProvider` is, step 122); its system instance is declared beside `ClockProvider.system` in step 239. No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests` (step 213), over a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive`: `an item's notes and photo are edited in place, keeping its parameters and revision`: `withNotes (ItemNotes "Mounted 2026-11-01")` and `withPhoto` of the kit path `data/photos/CPL1.jpg` (`KitRelativePath.tryCreate`, step 123) answer the item with those notes and that photo, and `withPhoto None` removes the photo; the parameters, revision 1 and the empty history are unchanged. `relabelling an item keeps its id and refuses a label whose file name another item holds`: over the items CPL1 and LP1 (an `ItemDraft` over `ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`), relabelling CPL1 `CPL 1` answers the item with its id and the new label, relabelling it `cpl1` answers that label, and relabelling it `lp1` answers `DuplicateItemLabelErr` naming `LP1`. `every item error renders its condition and its payload` (step 213) covers `UnknownKitItemErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the item edits land, `Item.withNotes` and `Item.withPhoto` MUST edit an item in place, `Item.relabelledAmong` MUST refuse a label whose file name another item holds, and `ItemError` MUST hold `UnknownKitItemErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item's notes and photo are edited in place, keeping its parameters and revision`, `relabelling an item keeps its id and refuses a label whose file name another item holds` and the widened `every item error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.
